# ARC-07: text is stored with LF in the repository (the index already is), so
# a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf cannot commit CRLF back. Shell scripts
# keep LF in the working tree too; PowerShell scripts keep CRLF.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.gz binary

# Store and check out binary assets byte for byte.
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true rewrites ASCII85-encoded PDFs with CRLF line
# endings on Windows checkouts. That changes each file's sha256 (so the document
# parse cache misses and a benchmark run silently re-parses with different OCR)
# and leaves PyMuPDF to repair the damaged files.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
